= Rig Landmarks =

#type: node
#context: sop
#internal: a3ob_rig_landmarks
#tags: arma, p3d

"""Places the landmarks of your character (chin, groin, shoulders, elbows, wrists, hips, knees, ankles) for Rig Fit, as positions that you drag in the viewport."""

Rig Fit fits the skeleton to 14 landmarks of your character: the chin, the groin, and the left and right shoulder, elbow, wrist, hip, knee and ankle. This node holds them as positions (X, Y, Z) that you place by hand. Put the node between your mesh and Rig Fit. Connect the skeleton and the sample body to its inputs 2 and 3 (the ones that go into Rig Fit) and press Guess Landmarks: it fills all 14 fields with the guess of Rig Fit. Then select the node, move the mouse over the viewport and press Enter: every landmark is a labelled marker that you drag. The markers are drawn on top of the mesh. A joint belongs inside the body; the chin and the groin are on the skin.

Mirror is on by default. Left is the +X side. The right markers follow the left ones, mirrored about the X = 0 plane, so dragging a left marker moves its right partner (the right fields cannot be edited then). Switch Mirror off to place both sides freely. To put a landmark back to the guess, choose it in the Landmark menu and press Guess This Landmark. To set a landmark from the mesh, select points in the viewport, choose the landmark in the Landmark menu and press Set From Selected Points: it takes the average of the points. Only the position is kept, not the selection. This is handy for the chin and the groin.

The node gives your mesh unchanged, with one detail vector per landmark that is set (a3ob_lm_chin and so on), which Rig Fit reads. A fresh node has no position set (all three numbers zero means not set); it warns and needs the guess. Rig Fit then guesses the landmarks that are not set.

@inputs

Your mesh:
    Your character mesh, the one that goes into Rig Fit. It comes out unchanged.

Skeleton:
    Optional. The Arma skeleton, for Guess Landmarks (the same one that goes into Rig Fit).

Sample body:
    Optional. The sample body with its bone weights, for Guess Landmarks (the same one that goes into Rig Fit).

@parameters

Guess Landmarks:
    #id: guess

    Fills all 14 positions with the auto-guess of Rig Fit for your mesh. Connect the skeleton to input 2 and the sample body to input 3 first. It replaces the positions that are set.

    Type: Button.

Mirror:
    #id: mirror

    Left is the +X side. On: the right landmarks follow the left ones, mirrored about the X = 0 plane, so dragging a left marker moves its right partner, and the right fields cannot be edited. Off: both sides are free.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Chin:
    #id: chin

    The tip of the chin. Its position (X, Y, Z). Drag its marker in the viewport (select the node, move the mouse over the viewport and press Enter), type the numbers, or use Guess Landmarks. All zero means not set: Rig Fit then guesses this landmark.

    Type: 3 numbers. Default: 0, 0, 0.

Groin:
    #id: groin

    The crotch, the highest point between the legs. Its position (X, Y, Z). Drag its marker in the viewport (select the node, move the mouse over the viewport and press Enter), type the numbers, or use Guess Landmarks. All zero means not set: Rig Fit then guesses this landmark.

    Type: 3 numbers. Default: 0, 0, 0.

Left Shoulder:
    #id: shoulder_l

    The left shoulder joint, inside the upper arm where it meets the body. Its position (X, Y, Z). Drag its marker in the viewport (select the node, move the mouse over the viewport and press Enter), type the numbers, or use Guess Landmarks. All zero means not set: Rig Fit then guesses this landmark.

    Type: 3 numbers. Default: 0, 0, 0.

Right Shoulder:
    #id: shoulder_r

    The right shoulder joint. Its position (X, Y, Z). Drag its marker in the viewport (select the node, move the mouse over the viewport and press Enter), type the numbers, or use Guess Landmarks. All zero means not set: Rig Fit then guesses this landmark. While Mirror is on this one follows the left side and cannot be edited.

    Type: 3 numbers. Default: 0, 0, 0. Editable when: Mirror is off.

Left Elbow:
    #id: elbow_l

    The left elbow joint, in the middle of the arm. Its position (X, Y, Z). Drag its marker in the viewport (select the node, move the mouse over the viewport and press Enter), type the numbers, or use Guess Landmarks. All zero means not set: Rig Fit then guesses this landmark.

    Type: 3 numbers. Default: 0, 0, 0.

Right Elbow:
    #id: elbow_r

    The right elbow joint. Its position (X, Y, Z). Drag its marker in the viewport (select the node, move the mouse over the viewport and press Enter), type the numbers, or use Guess Landmarks. All zero means not set: Rig Fit then guesses this landmark. While Mirror is on this one follows the left side and cannot be edited.

    Type: 3 numbers. Default: 0, 0, 0. Editable when: Mirror is off.

Left Wrist:
    #id: wrist_l

    The left wrist joint, in the middle of the arm. Its position (X, Y, Z). Drag its marker in the viewport (select the node, move the mouse over the viewport and press Enter), type the numbers, or use Guess Landmarks. All zero means not set: Rig Fit then guesses this landmark.

    Type: 3 numbers. Default: 0, 0, 0.

Right Wrist:
    #id: wrist_r

    The right wrist joint. Its position (X, Y, Z). Drag its marker in the viewport (select the node, move the mouse over the viewport and press Enter), type the numbers, or use Guess Landmarks. All zero means not set: Rig Fit then guesses this landmark. While Mirror is on this one follows the left side and cannot be edited.

    Type: 3 numbers. Default: 0, 0, 0. Editable when: Mirror is off.

Left Hip:
    #id: hip_l

    The left hip joint, inside the top of the thigh. Its position (X, Y, Z). Drag its marker in the viewport (select the node, move the mouse over the viewport and press Enter), type the numbers, or use Guess Landmarks. All zero means not set: Rig Fit then guesses this landmark.

    Type: 3 numbers. Default: 0, 0, 0.

Right Hip:
    #id: hip_r

    The right hip joint. Its position (X, Y, Z). Drag its marker in the viewport (select the node, move the mouse over the viewport and press Enter), type the numbers, or use Guess Landmarks. All zero means not set: Rig Fit then guesses this landmark. While Mirror is on this one follows the left side and cannot be edited.

    Type: 3 numbers. Default: 0, 0, 0. Editable when: Mirror is off.

Left Knee:
    #id: knee_l

    The left knee joint, in the middle of the leg. Its position (X, Y, Z). Drag its marker in the viewport (select the node, move the mouse over the viewport and press Enter), type the numbers, or use Guess Landmarks. All zero means not set: Rig Fit then guesses this landmark.

    Type: 3 numbers. Default: 0, 0, 0.

Right Knee:
    #id: knee_r

    The right knee joint. Its position (X, Y, Z). Drag its marker in the viewport (select the node, move the mouse over the viewport and press Enter), type the numbers, or use Guess Landmarks. All zero means not set: Rig Fit then guesses this landmark. While Mirror is on this one follows the left side and cannot be edited.

    Type: 3 numbers. Default: 0, 0, 0. Editable when: Mirror is off.

Left Ankle:
    #id: ankle_l

    The left ankle joint, in the middle of the leg. Its position (X, Y, Z). Drag its marker in the viewport (select the node, move the mouse over the viewport and press Enter), type the numbers, or use Guess Landmarks. All zero means not set: Rig Fit then guesses this landmark.

    Type: 3 numbers. Default: 0, 0, 0.

Right Ankle:
    #id: ankle_r

    The right ankle joint. Its position (X, Y, Z). Drag its marker in the viewport (select the node, move the mouse over the viewport and press Enter), type the numbers, or use Guess Landmarks. All zero means not set: Rig Fit then guesses this landmark. While Mirror is on this one follows the left side and cannot be edited.

    Type: 3 numbers. Default: 0, 0, 0. Editable when: Mirror is off.

Match Left to Right:
    #id: leftToRight

    Once: puts each right landmark at the mirror image of its left partner (mirrored about X = 0, Left is +X). Chin and groin stay as they are, and a left landmark that is not set is skipped. Disabled while Mirror is on, because the right side already follows the left.

    Type: Button. Editable when: Mirror is off.

Match Right to Left:
    #id: rightToLeft

    Once: puts each left landmark at the mirror image of its right partner (mirrored about X = 0, Left is +X). Chin and groin stay as they are, and a right landmark that is not set is skipped. With Mirror on, the right side then follows the new left side.

    Type: Button.

Landmark:
    #id: which

    The landmark that the two buttons below work on.

    Type: Menu. Default: Chin.

    Choices: Chin, Groin, Left Shoulder, Right Shoulder, Left Elbow, Right Elbow, Left Wrist, Right Wrist, Left Hip, Right Hip, Left Knee, Right Knee, Left Ankle, Right Ankle.

Guess This Landmark:
    #id: guessone

    Puts the landmark chosen above back to its auto-guess (needs inputs 2 and 3 like Guess Landmarks). With Mirror on, its partner follows.

    Type: Button.

Set From Selected Points:
    #id: fromsel

    Puts the landmark chosen above at the average of the points that are selected in the viewport. Only the position is kept, not the selection. Useful for the chin and the groin. With Mirror on, its partner follows.

    Type: Button.

The full page for this node is docs/user/reference/a3ob_rig_landmarks.html in the A3OB folder. Open it in a web browser.
